From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:20:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 09/55] ssh: do not disable the none switch for -T

The none cipher is only allowed on sessions without a tty, and the comment
says -T was meant to stop it on an interactive session. But -T asks for no
tty, which is the case it is allowed in, so "ssh -T -oNoneSwitch=yes" always
lost it. Disable it for -t instead, the interactive case.

Changelog: sphynx 0.2.4

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ssh.c | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ssh.c b/ssh.c
index 06cddbed6..ae842cecc 100644
--- a/ssh.c
+++ b/ssh.c
@@ -892,6 +892,13 @@ main(int ac, char **av)
 				options.request_tty = REQUEST_TTY_FORCE;
 			else
 				options.request_tty = REQUEST_TTY_YES;
+			/*
+			 * ensure that the user doesn't try to backdoor a null cipher
+			 * switch on an interactive session, so explicitly disable it
+			 * no matter what. (-T asks for no tty, which is the case the
+			 * none cipher is allowed in, so it must not disable it.)
+			 */
+			options.none_switch = 0;
 			break;
 		case 'v':
 			if (debug_flag == 0) {
@@ -1050,10 +1057,6 @@ main(int ac, char **av)
 			break;
 		case 'T':
 			options.request_tty = REQUEST_TTY_NO;
-			/* ensure that the user doesn't try to backdoor a */
-			/* null cipher switch on an interactive session */
-			/* so explicitly disable it no matter what */
-			options.none_switch=0;
 			break;
 		case 'o':
 			line = xstrdup(optarg);
-- 
